			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Normalize Unicode whitespace in Architecture documentation\n\nStandardize the use of Unicode whitespace characters (specifically the em space \\u2009) between section headers and icons in `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md`. Ensure consistent spacing across all headers (Overview, Architecture, Module Map, etc.) to align with the project's strict documentation formatting conventions established in recent commits.\n\nThis cleanup resolves visual inconsistencies in the rendered GitHub README and maintains uniformity with other architectural documentation in the Wind service layer.",
			"SHA": "333c3023c5b887790ac025d9a93a9ac8778fe6c6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T23:36:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1929,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Standardize architecture documentation with unicode section icons and inline code\n\nRefactor the `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file to align with the project's strict formatting conventions. Replace plain text references with backtick-wrapped inline code for all technical identifiers (e.g., `Wind`, `Mountain`, `Tauri`, `Effect-TS`). Add Unicode section icons (🍃, 📋, 🏗️, 🗺️, etc.) to headers for improved visual navigation in the GitHub README view.\n\nAdditionally, update the \"Related Documentation\" links to use absolute HTTPS URLs pointing to the `Current` branch on GitHub, ensuring external navigation reliability, and adjust table column widths for consistent alignment. These changes enhance the document's readability and ensure strict adherence to the documentation style guide.",
			"SHA": "d899f5598f8f33aa037ceca14686e0c0c9c24593"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:32:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1929,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Add comprehensive architecture diagram\n\nSupplement the `Architecture.md` documentation with a detailed Mermaid graph illustrating the Wind Frontend Service Layer structure.\n\nThe diagram visualizes the `Preload.ts` shim, the categorized Effect services (Core, Editor, File System, UI, Misc), and the Layer composition strategy (`TauriLiveLayer`, `ElectronLiveLayer`, `TestLayer`). It also clarifies the data flow to the Mountain backend via Tauri and consumption by the Sky UI layer.\n\nThis addition provides a clear visual reference for the architectural boundaries and component interactions within the Wind service layer.",
			"SHA": "6e5c80e5118bb0bcb4aac44ecb9c0ab7a1aa95c1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:24:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1929,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Add comprehensive architecture documentation\n\nIntroduce the `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file to describe the Wind UI service layer. This document details the Effect-TS native implementation that replaces VS Code's Electron IPC pipeline with typed Tauri commands routed to the Mountain Rust backend.\n\nKey contents include:\n- Overview of the `Preload.ts` shim and `Effect/` service modules.\n- Explanation of the Define/Implement/Problem pattern for service construction.\n- Description of Layer composition (`TauriLiveLayer`, `ElectronLiveLayer`, `TestLayer`).\n- Mapping of Wind services to Mountain Tauri commands via `Effect/Mountain.ts`.\n- Integration flows with the VS Code workbench and Sky UI component layer.\n\nThis documentation serves as the primary reference for the frontend service contracts and architectural boundaries between Wind, Mountain, and Sky.",
			"SHA": "24549234b966e7bf7453cd490ea6ea17a22b2f72"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T19:12:44Z",
